==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Raijin Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kabuto Cat's usage is rather high due to its strong attributes and how easily accessible the unit is. Since it is given for free in the beginning of the game, the player is essentially given a bulky, high damaging unit without much commitment. Though its usage dwindles somewhat in the Empire of Cats chapter and in the other [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]] as there are much better alternatives, it can then serve its main purpose of being a specialized meatshield towards [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]]. It is essentially a budget version of either [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]] or [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Li'l Gau]], as it suffices in its role albeit not as great as the units mentioned earlier. Since this unit is in collaboration with CoroCoro, Kabuto Cat's XP costs are low compared to most units, making it easy to achieve [[User Rank]] rewards.

Strategizing with Kabuto Cat is rather simple, use when Dark Enemies are present. Since it has comparable stats that to a Level 30 Nono CC, it serves as a capable anti-Dark meatshield and can hold off the line due to its 40,600 effective HP at max level. Since it does have a sluggish cooldown with about 9 to 6 seconds, it is advised to bring additional meatshields to help defend incoming enemies.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield & User Rank Dump}}

