==Trivia==
*Kabuto Cat is named after [[:wikipedia:Kabuto|kabuto]], a type of helmet worn by Japanese warriors.
*The attack animation from Kabuto Cat emits small electricity from where it bites.
*It and Kuwagata Cat are currently the only Switch-Exclusive Special Cats to be obtainable for free via an update.
*It, [[Kuwagata Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kuwagata Cat]], [[Corodragon (Switch Special Cat)|Corodragon]], [[Undies Cat Jr. (Switch Special Cat)|Undies Cat Jr.]], [[Manga Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Cat]], [[Manga Boogie Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Boogie Cat]], and [[Manga Darabotchgogogo Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Darabotchgogogo Cat]] are Japanese exclusives to The Battle Cats Unite.
*Kabuto Cat gains a [[Kabuto Cat (Special Cat)|mobile counterpart]] in the [[Summer Break Cats]] event with slightly altered designs. Its mobile version also Resists [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, however, it trades its Resist ability for Strong but gains Immune to Slow.
*Prior to [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.9 Update|Patch 1.0.9]], Kabuto Cat's description stated it targeted Black enemies instead of Dark.
*Prior to [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.3 Update/WW|Patch 1.0.3]] on the International version, this was Kabuto Cat's original description:
<pre>Cat with an awesome homemade battle helmet.
It's made of styrofoam, but still pretty heavy.
Tough vs Dark enemies.</pre>
<pre>Helm has been blessed by the God of Thunder!
Turned bright red after infusion of battle power!
Tough vs Dark enemies.</pre>

